# G4/G24 (wt-s3scope, "G4 for constants"): a constant variable no parameter can give a value is one error at the
# declaration, "the body unchecked and calls silent" - true for a plain function (mk), but a generic one (mk2, which also
# has a type variable) is instantiated anyway and its body checked, adding a second, misleading error (G21: "a constant
# argument must be computable while compiling ...") at the body, with an "instantiated here" note at the call.
# expected: exactly two errors, the two G4/G24 at lines 7 and 11
# actual:   a third, error[G21] at 12:16, plus "note: instantiated here, with T = I32"
fn mk() Array<I64, <N>> {
    a Array<I64, N>
    return a
}
fn mk2(x <T>) Array<T, <N I64>> {
    a Array<T, N>
    return a
}
fn main() ? {
    a := mk()
    b := mk2(3)
    println($a.Len() " " $b.Len())
}
